  "body": "As per the discussion in [bz1593064](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1593064), there are presently interop issues with which page scroll state is being restored when users press back/forward (etc). For instance, pages which call `window.scroll(0,0)` may be ignored on Chrome, but not on Firefox, leading to users reporting webcompat issues such as [this one with ABC News](https://webcompat.com/issues/33753). To prevent this kind of issue, it seems worth aligning on which scroll state ought to be restored and when.",
